 "comments": {
  "32895923-afdf-4f29-82f4-9bead4287d00": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p3-definition",
     "replacement": "Data has **variables and values.**\n\n- **A variable** is anything we can describe, measure, or count.\n- **Data values** are the values a variable takes.\n\n**Variables**\t**Data values**\nAge\t11, 12, 15, 21, 86\nGrade\tA, B, C, D, E\nColour\tRed, Green, Orange\n\nA **random variable**, $X$, is a variable whose values $x$ are **outcomes** of a random process.\n\nThe outcomes of a random variable are **always numbers.**\n\n**Random variable **$X$\t**Data values / Outcomes **$x$\nNumber rolled on a standard die.\t$\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}$\nNumber of heads when tossing a coin three times.\t$\\{0,1,2,3\\}$\nHeight of a Year 7 student in Mr Ding’s class, in cm.\t$\\{x:120<x<155\\}$",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p3-definition",
     "targetFingerprint": "bc6c663d26da68d778fbcb8b162d99a4e0456d051e3074093feebeab4388d604",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-probability-and-data-4-data-v1/20261111-080708",
   "revision": 18
  },
  "d21a7e15-52e2-40f0-8fec-15311b31ab86": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p6-frequency-definition",
     "replacement": "**Frequency** is how often a data value occurs.\n\nA **frequency histogram** is a column graph with one column for each data value. Each column is centred on its value and has height equal to the frequency. Columns touch, so a value with frequency 0 has a column of zero height.\n\nA **frequency polygon** joins the centres of the tops of the histogram columns with straight lines and extends to the $x$-axis at a zero-frequency value one interval beyond each end.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p6-frequency-definition",
     "targetFingerprint": "08b56dfc095615d507db32f5d1e273b316e5fb0d2622140e85bfb84ac82ca4e2",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-probability-and-data-4-data-v1/20261111-080708",
   "revision": 18
  },
  "b219b48e-031c-44ee-91d9-452ab84dead3": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p9-theory",
     "replacement": "A **cumulative frequency histogram** is a histogram whose column heights are the cumulative frequencies.\n\nA **cumulative frequency polygon**, or **ogive**, is a line graph that starts at the bottom-left corner of the first column and connects the **top-right corners** of the columns.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p9-theory",
     "targetFingerprint": "3b199f3803d46c0fdf388bd677297844fd176e3bad1e74fc690c8b42b0fb4313",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-probability-and-data-4-data-v1/20261111-080708",
   "revision": 18
  },
  "6b554f89-591c-47a2-8504-a263e9ad19b8": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p10-definition",
     "replacement": "The **mode** is the data value that appears **most often** in a dataset. If two or more values tie for the greatest frequency, each of them is a mode.\n\nThe mode is the data value, not its frequency.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p10-definition",
     "targetFingerprint": "a73f1081be9d98234700abd73685478d786a71a50d463020349e3845dd59eaa3",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-probability-and-data-4-data-v1/20261111-080708",
   "revision": 18
  },
  "c4dce5d6-4e89-4c0f-8820-a5d67633995d": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p14-definition",
     "replacement": "The **relative frequency** of an outcome is the fraction of all trials in which the outcome happens.\n\n$$\\begin{gathered}\\text{Relative}\\\\\\text{frequency}\\end{gathered}=\\frac{\\text{Frequency of outcome}}{\\text{Total frequency}}$$\n\nThe relative frequencies of all outcomes must add to 1.\n\nWhen graphing, it is a good idea to express relative frequency as a decimal.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p14-definition",
     "targetFingerprint": "c00a387c0f75c06ecafaed6ffc9c1cbd4ee5bc95018c5ad1031a48699a180414",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-probability-and-data-4-data-v1/20261111-080708",
   "revision": 18
  },
